======================================================================================================================
(2) WHAT DOES THE ESTIMATOR RETURN WHEN THERE IS NO CURVE?
======================================================================================================================
  s21's shuffle null sat at 1.800-1.809 on every powered stack, and the
  Gaussian value is 1.8226. Is that a coincidence, or is ~1.80 simply what
  a structureless narrow blob returns? Pure noise, no curve, 400 draws:
    K=  19  median 1.5806  sd 0.7116  n 252/400   |median - Gaussian| = 0.2420
    K=  33  median 1.6444  sd 0.9465  n 313/400   |median - Gaussian| = 0.1782
    K= 105  median 1.6809  sd 0.6756  n 359/400   |median - Gaussian| = 0.1417
    K= 299  median 1.7800  sd 0.9812  n 375/400   |median - Gaussian| = 0.0426

  structureless floor = 1.6627   Gaussian = 1.8226   separation = 0.1599
  The pre-registered bar is 0.11. The floor is 0.1599 from the
  Gaussian value, i.e. INSIDE the bar. A stack reading 'Gaussian' therefore
  cannot be distinguished from a stack reading NOTHING.

